        "original_id": "1f6f5ee9-8508-5c5a-be3f-a3904e9f0a1f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Linda Eder, Robert Louis Stevenson, Frank Wildhorn, Steve Cuden, Leslie Bricusse\n- Works: Jekyll & Hyde, The Strange Case of Dr Jekyll and Mr Hyde\n- Roles: Lucy\n- Topics: Broadway, musical theater, horror-drama\n\nFacts:\n- Linda Eder, born on February 3, 1961, is an American singer and actress.\n- Linda Eder made her Broadway debut in the musical Jekyll & Hyde, where she originated the role of Lucy and received a Drama Desk Award nomination.\n- Jekyll & Hyde is a musical horror-drama loosely based on Robert Louis Stevenson's novella The Strange Case of Dr Jekyll and Mr Hyde.\n- Jekyll & Hyde was originally conceived for the stage by Frank Wildhorn and Steve Cuden.\n- Jekyll & Hyde features music by Frank Wildhorn, a book by Leslie Bricusse, and lyrics by Frank Wildhorn, Leslie Bricusse, and Steve Cuden.",
